Result: exit 0. The script passed the existing source, missing-Message expiry, and scheduled-Message expiry response-loss cases, then passed the new Target Admission case against three KRaft Brokers. The OffsetCommit proxy recorded Broker responses received and withheld in every case.

For `TARGET_PUBLISH_ADMISSION`, the source records were a root grant at offset 0, Target grant at offset 1, membership at offset 2, Schedule at offset 3, and signed Target Admission bodyVersion 3 / tuple `(1,1,SYSTEM_MUTATION,1,3)` at offset 4. The Worker applied Admission to RocksDB before the proxy withheld the Broker OffsetCommit response. The group offset was 5 (the next offset after record 4); the exact pending source entry remained `ACK_UNKNOWN`. The Store contained the PUBLISHING Message and deterministic attempt, an ADMITTED `TargetQuotaAttemptBudget`, and the immutable system-result and source-position records, while the consumed Claim and Claim charge were absent. The same Host retried only ACK after proxy release: the source turn completed as `APPLIED_AND_ACKED`, RocksDB sequence and Shard mutation sequence did not increase, the Broker group offset stayed 5, and Admission authority resolution stayed at one.

This smoke uses explicit test signing, Owner lease, tuple, and time/evidence authorities, plus a test-created Claim. It exercises a real locked K1 Kafka cluster, the real Kafka source client/Worker, and a local RocksDB Store. It does not establish production Owner/history authority assembly, Producer-send integration, Target Outcome handling, process restart/recovery, or centralized E5 validation. Registry PUBLISH_ADMISSION v1 remains unchanged.

